 name of the solid shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The solid is a **right cone**. \n\nNotice the following:\n\n- The solid has one circular base and one vertex. So, it's a cone.\n\n- The axis that passes through the center of the circle and the vertex is perpendicular to the base. So, it's right."} :step/id #uuid "87f1f045-6509-52aa-9286-2d5c94a46705" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414716}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414718 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147900 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1900d6b5-ab4e-5cb6-875c-d1325629dba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Cube" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414681} {:answer/id #uuid "332e4dbe-20b8-54c1-9358-14a060035cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Pentagonal prism" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414686} {:answer/id #uuid "58cc569c-846f-5023-b24c-d641fdf00ece" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Triangular pyramid" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414693} {:answer/id #uuid "598ea44a-33fd-558b-a72c-9415a8e71931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Pentagonal pyramid" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414694} {:answer/id #uuid "e6a1f23e-e7bc-5e52-a9a0-4fe70a04cb29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Rectangular prism" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414703}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414694} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5df61c8-1685-5b05-bfab-2db504a8dcb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0def774f-f257-5952-add7-f3a6aeb741ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-61656" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c73b984b3e4a2ccb0796646ebb4c547947fab7359914599d928a63819818725.png)\n\nWhat is the name of the polyhedron shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The solid is a **pentagonal pyramid** since it is a pyramid whose base is a pentagon.\n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a triangular pyramid since not all its faces are triangular.\n\n- The solid is not a pentagonal prism since it has only one pentagonal face.\n\n- The solid is not a rectangular prism since not all of its faces are rectangles. Due to the same reasons, the solid is not a cube."} :step/id #uuid "d58ea3ef-a954-5458-b665-9faf042fb48e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414715}}] :activity/title "Identifying Three-Dimensional Shapes" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414679}]}
